# Build context for the hosted image. The app reads its artifacts from the
# repository root, so the container is a copy of the repo with the parts it
# never opens removed. Sizes and reasoning are in docs/deployment.md.

# --- Large artifacts the serving app never reads -----------------------------

# 536 MB of OSDR counts matrices, read only by the `subprocess` retrieval tier.
# That tier is empty whenever the cache exists: sample_tier() returns `cached`
# before it looks at a counts path, and the 55 samples that do reach
# _counts_columns() are already classified `unavailable` either way, because a
# missing file yields an empty frozenset. Excluding this changes no tier.
data/osdr/raw/

# 122 MB precompute intermediate that makes a re-embed cheap. The container
# never re-embeds the corpus.
cache/osdr_expression.float32.npy
cache/osdr_sample_embeddings.partial.f32
cache/osdr_sample_embeddings.progress.json

# --- Local environment, never part of an image -------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

.git/
.gitattributes
.github/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.serena/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*Zone.Identifier*

reports/
*.log

# A candidate projection build kept for comparison; not what the app serves.
cache_compare_nn15/

# --- Not needed to serve -----------------------------------------------------
# The browser checks drive a running app from outside it, and the unit tests
# build their own synthetic corpus. Neither belongs in the runtime image.
tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
